    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42114" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sābātīnus</span></b>  (<b>poet.</b>
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sābātĭus</span></b> ), a, um,
			adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Sabate</i>
			(a town of Etruria): lacus, <i>the Lake of Sabate</i>,
			now <i>Lago di Bracciano</i>, <i><span class="en">Front.
				Aquaed. 71</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 8, 16, 2</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">called lacus Sabate,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Fest. p. 343</span></i>
			
			 Müll.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sabatina tribus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 6,
					5 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Fest. l. l.—Form Sabatius: stagna,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					8, 492</span></i>
			.</div>
